WEBVTT

00:04.930 --> 00:08.400
Pardon me for asking, but how old are you?

00:08.400 --> 00:11.680
These tense, bottled-up emotions...

00:11.680 --> 00:15.910
Rather than detract, they bring an energy 
that befits a young writer.

00:16.760 --> 00:18.660
The overall aim of the plot is interesting,

00:18.980 --> 00:22.290
but it feels overcomplicated, 
with too many extraneous elements.

00:22.840 --> 00:25.670
This sort of melodrama doesn't really 
suit someone of your stature.

00:26.020 --> 00:29.940
The speech, mannerisms, and perspectives 
of the characters really reflect this era.

00:29.940 --> 00:33.180
And the themes have a universality to them.

00:35.520 --> 00:39.280
The themes are run-of-the-mill, 
and the premise isn't convincing.

00:39.560 --> 00:42.160
You're only writing to 
suit yourself, aren't you?

00:42.160 --> 00:45.070
I think you need a more innovative angle.

00:49.110 --> 00:52.420
<i>Pardon me for asking, but how old are you?</i>

01:00.690 --> 01:05.670
Happy 28th birthday, me.

01:03.830 --> 01:06.960
<b>Happy 28th Birthday, Me</b>

01:11.550 --> 01:16.350
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

01:11.550 --> 01:16.350
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

02:40.450 --> 02:42.020
<i>A Juusho, is it?</i>

02:40.470 --> 02:47.230
<b>Schoolhouse, Drool, and an Apartment Wife</b>

02:40.470 --> 02:47.250
<b>Schoolhouse, Drool, and an Apartment Wife</b>

02:42.700 --> 02:48.060
<i>This can be exchanged for 
one ticket to Yami Station.</i>

02:48.580 --> 02:50.580
<i>I won't this time, thank you.</i>

02:51.470 --> 02:53.650
<i>That's a shame.</i>

02:55.070 --> 02:58.070
<b>KISARAGI</b>

03:01.030 --> 03:03.550
<i>You couldn't get a ticket?</i>

03:03.550 --> 03:06.880
<i>It wasn't enough. They ordered me 
to go look for more Curiosities.</i>

03:07.260 --> 03:09.590
<i>You know how spiteful 
they are at this station.</i>

03:10.270 --> 03:12.070
<i>I'm back, Oto.</i>

03:11.800 --> 03:13.590
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

03:11.800 --> 03:13.590
<b>Adashino Oto</b>

03:14.400 --> 03:16.590
<i>It might be a while longer 
before you can go home.</i>

03:17.700 --> 03:18.840
<i>But...</i>

03:19.810 --> 03:23.310
<i>No matter what it takes, 
I will return you to your world.</i>

03:23.310 --> 03:26.790
<i>Ren-nii, let's go back together, okay?</i>

03:28.100 --> 03:31.820
<i>Oh. I forgot about Sumireko-san.</i>

03:32.240 --> 03:36.220
<i>About that... Is she your girlfriend?</i>

03:36.220 --> 03:37.730
<i>Of course not.</i>

03:37.730 --> 03:39.800
<i>She's my senpai from work.</i>

03:39.800 --> 03:41.620
<i>You could say she's done a lot for me.</i>

03:42.520 --> 03:46.120
<i>But then she got mixed up 
with a Curiosity and nearly died.</i>

03:46.120 --> 03:47.730
<i>I couldn't just stand by and watch.</i>

03:50.710 --> 03:53.390
First, we need to do something 
about these panties on display.

03:53.660 --> 03:56.390
Oto, do you have any spare clothes with you?

03:57.680 --> 03:59.890
Huh? Are you angry?

04:03.430 --> 04:05.940
Will that butt even fit in these?

04:06.430 --> 04:07.640
<i>Ren-nii.</i>

04:08.720 --> 04:11.140
<i>Are you going to look for another Curiosity?</i>

04:11.450 --> 04:12.940
<i>Of course I am.</i>

04:14.420 --> 04:17.030
<i>I might know of one.</i>

04:17.030 --> 04:18.150
<i>Where?</i>

04:18.640 --> 04:20.660
<i>My school.</i>

04:24.890 --> 04:26.630
Koone Girls' Academy?

04:27.410 --> 04:30.420
"You... grow older..."

04:30.420 --> 04:31.920
She just...

04:46.560 --> 04:48.460
Did you put them on?

04:48.460 --> 04:52.730
Since you're the one asking, 
I'm not against doing this, but...

04:53.890 --> 04:56.470
Is this <i>really</i> necessary?

04:57.070 --> 04:59.090
That works surprisingly well.

05:00.410 --> 05:03.790
Why do you even have a uniform like this?

05:03.790 --> 05:06.950
Starting today, I'd like you to 
become one of Oto's friends.

05:08.550 --> 05:11.960
Hey. You owe me an explanation, youngster.

05:11.960 --> 05:14.840
<b>K</b>

05:11.960 --> 05:14.840
<b>I</b>

05:11.960 --> 05:14.840
<b>S</b>

05:11.960 --> 05:14.840
<b>A</b>

05:11.960 --> 05:14.840
<b>R</b>

05:11.960 --> 05:14.840
<b>A</b>

05:11.960 --> 05:14.840
<b>G</b>

05:11.960 --> 05:14.840
<b>I</b>

05:13.470 --> 05:14.840
Curiosities?

05:14.840 --> 05:20.080
Yes. For example, you've heard of mysterious 
disappearances caused by spirits, right?

05:20.080 --> 05:24.090
Oh, kamikakushi? There was 
a famous one described in...

05:24.090 --> 05:28.220
Hirata Atsutane's <i>Senkyou Ibun</i>.

05:24.260 --> 05:25.850
<b>\hSenkyou Ibun\h</b>

05:28.220 --> 05:31.230
You're as well-read as 
I'd expect, Sumireko-san.

05:32.690 --> 05:36.330
I believe that the ones 
spirited away in this fashion

05:36.670 --> 05:41.610
may be those deemed unnecessary 
in their original world.

05:43.910 --> 05:47.430
What are you planning to make me do?

05:49.460 --> 05:52.770
My little sister Oto attends 
Koone Girls' Academy,

05:52.770 --> 05:55.830
where it seems that troublesome 
phenomena have been taking place.

05:55.830 --> 05:59.150
I want to help her, but as it's an 
all-girls school, my hands are tied.

06:00.260 --> 06:06.760
So I'd like you to pose as a friend of Oto's 
and infiltrate the school in my place.

06:13.820 --> 06:15.890
All right. I'll do it.

06:15.890 --> 06:16.540
What?

06:17.070 --> 06:20.760
Are you sure? It's a totally unreasonable 
request, if I do say so myself.

06:20.760 --> 06:23.820
Uh, I don't think you should
be saying that yourself.

06:23.820 --> 06:25.100
So why, then?

06:25.910 --> 06:29.060
I am the author Ogawa Sumireko.

06:29.550 --> 06:31.910
That's enough reason in itself, isn't it?

06:38.750 --> 06:43.150
That said, I think squeezing 
into this uniform is a lost cause.

06:43.150 --> 06:44.170
Any other ideas?

06:44.660 --> 06:48.180
I do believe we have a 
light of hope in that regard.

06:48.740 --> 06:52.680
In taking on the poem's curse, you have 
become a curse of sorts yourself—

06:53.270 --> 06:55.690
a "Bearer of Youth," if you will.

06:53.640 --> 06:55.690
<b>\hBearer of Youth\h</b>

06:56.370 --> 07:00.940
As such, Sumireko-san, you should be able 
to freely invoke the transformation.

07:00.940 --> 07:02.070
What?

07:02.070 --> 07:04.320
Even into a high schooler.

07:04.320 --> 07:05.290
What?

07:05.820 --> 07:09.360
Try standing there and reciting the spell.

07:09.730 --> 07:11.480
All right, but...

07:13.020 --> 07:17.830
"In the heavens, the sun and moon shine. 
You are like them in my thoughts,

07:18.260 --> 07:21.950
and I regret that with each 
new day, you grow older."

07:24.330 --> 07:25.870
Looks like it succeeded.

07:28.220 --> 07:31.620
You've lost that sexy, 
older woman appeal, though.

07:31.620 --> 07:32.690
Hey.

07:32.690 --> 07:35.000
You could stand to sound 
a little happier about it.

08:29.100 --> 08:30.550
Where is this place?

08:35.860 --> 08:40.420
Koone Girls' Academy is a prestigious school, 
founded over a hundred years ago.

08:40.730 --> 08:42.320
It's a combined middle and high school,

08:42.320 --> 08:46.170
and students can enroll at any level, 
so it should be easy to slip in.

08:49.080 --> 08:53.180
<i>They have a rigorous school culture 
that honors public morals and tradition,</i>

08:53.180 --> 08:56.350
<i>but currently, they have been experiencing 
a series of inexplicable phenomena—</i>

08:56.350 --> 08:59.180
<i>no, inexplicable incidents.</i>

08:59.180 --> 09:00.720
Good day to you.

09:00.720 --> 09:01.630
Oh.

09:01.940 --> 09:03.310
Good mor—

09:04.320 --> 09:09.440
Oto-chan, that young man was so captivated 
by you that he walked into a signpost.

09:09.910 --> 09:13.070
Along the path to school, running 
straight along an embankment,

09:13.070 --> 09:16.110
a multitude of cultured young 
ladies walk in procession.

09:17.280 --> 09:20.080
What a sight for sore eyes 
this school commute is!

09:20.820 --> 09:24.220
Can you feel the tsunami of youth, Oto-chan?

09:24.220 --> 09:25.270
Yes.

09:25.270 --> 09:30.460
It feels like the opening scene from an old 
TV drama that exemplifies adolescence! Right?

09:30.460 --> 09:31.550
Um...

09:33.290 --> 09:36.830
Could you not be quite so 
familiar with me... please?

09:36.830 --> 09:40.100
Huh? Sure... Huh?

09:40.100 --> 09:41.960
Occhan!

09:43.910 --> 09:45.200
Good day to you!

09:45.200 --> 09:47.960
Good day to you, Nodoka, Mari.

09:47.960 --> 09:50.460
Occhan, who is this?

09:50.460 --> 09:53.160
Oh, nice to meet you! I'm—

09:53.160 --> 09:55.680
This is Wakazukuri-senpai.

09:55.680 --> 09:56.460
Huh?

09:56.870 --> 10:00.020
P-Pardon me for not knowing, 
Wakazukuri-senpai!

10:00.900 --> 10:02.240
We must hurry!

10:02.240 --> 10:03.090
Yes!

10:07.880 --> 10:10.150
I will never accept someone like you.

10:10.970 --> 10:13.850
Stop i-ingratiating yourself with Ren-nii!

10:13.850 --> 10:15.010
I'm...

10:15.010 --> 10:17.010
You... lonely apartment wife!

10:17.560 --> 10:19.540
L-Lonely...

10:24.900 --> 10:27.520
If I've done something to offend you, 
please let me apologize!

10:27.520 --> 10:32.690
Even so, though! That's no reason to call 
someone an "apartment wife" as an insult!

10:38.390 --> 10:39.530
<i>Incidents?</i>

10:40.010 --> 10:44.330
<i>Several students have failed to attend 
classes for rather peculiar reasons.</i>

10:40.070 --> 10:48.540
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

10:40.450 --> 10:48.540
<b>Koone Girls' Academy</b>

10:44.330 --> 10:47.780
<i>It's quite likely that a Curiosity 
is involved in some way.</i>

10:49.520 --> 10:50.710
<i>Sumireko-san,</i>

10:51.390 --> 10:54.290
<i>please go and ascertain the truth 
behind these incidents.</i>

10:57.990 --> 11:00.340
Good day to you, Onee-sama.

11:00.340 --> 11:01.620
Good day to you.

11:02.160 --> 11:03.060
What's this?

11:03.370 --> 11:05.560
Your ribbon is crooked.

11:09.900 --> 11:12.810
Don't stare like that.

11:13.160 --> 11:16.420
Oh, Adashino-san. Good day to you.

11:16.420 --> 11:19.830
G-Good day to you, Uname-sensei.

11:19.610 --> 11:21.330
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

11:19.990 --> 11:21.330
<b>Uname Manami</b>

11:20.350 --> 11:21.330
What's this?

11:21.630 --> 11:24.140
Senpai, we have to go, or else...

11:25.580 --> 11:27.700
Are you...

11:27.700 --> 11:28.580
Huh?

11:29.400 --> 11:33.710
I'm so sorry. What was your name again?

11:33.710 --> 11:36.040
This is Wakazukuri-senpai.

11:36.040 --> 11:37.470
If you'll excuse us...

11:42.620 --> 11:44.730
Apartment wife...

11:45.270 --> 11:48.290
Just stay here until after school.

11:48.890 --> 11:49.980
Huh?

11:49.980 --> 11:52.470
You can't be serious!

11:57.990 --> 12:00.990
<b>OUT OF ORDER</b>

12:06.180 --> 12:07.580
Apartment wife.

12:07.580 --> 12:10.250
Oh, Oto-chan.

12:11.520 --> 12:12.660
I...

12:12.970 --> 12:14.000
I...

12:14.850 --> 12:18.600
I planned to spend the day chattering gaily 
with beautiful middle and high school girls.

12:19.110 --> 12:24.010
So why have I instead spent the last 
six hours and fifty-one minutes

12:24.010 --> 12:28.580
thoroughly acquainting my rump 
with every contour of this toilet seat?!

12:30.360 --> 12:31.330
Here.

12:34.330 --> 12:38.100
We're at an all-girls school, and you're 
telling me to eat in the bathroom?

12:38.720 --> 12:40.910
What happened to chattering gaily?

12:40.910 --> 12:43.410
That wasn't part of the plan.

12:43.410 --> 12:44.720
And it never will be.

12:45.660 --> 12:47.040
Never?

12:49.900 --> 12:51.170
Wait, please!

12:52.880 --> 12:54.420
Where are you going?

12:54.420 --> 12:56.810
A place where a Curiosity probably was.

12:56.810 --> 12:59.050
"Probably was"?

13:05.790 --> 13:06.680
Here.

13:07.170 --> 13:10.220
There's a sign here that something happened.

13:11.710 --> 13:13.640
I don't see anything.

13:14.150 --> 13:15.690
I knew you wouldn't.

13:17.740 --> 13:20.200
I won't make fun of you. Just tell me.

13:20.500 --> 13:23.260
I love these kinds of stories!

13:25.250 --> 13:26.950
The thing that's here...

13:27.360 --> 13:30.960
is a trace left behind by something that 
happened—a sense of something wrong.

13:31.710 --> 13:35.570
By way of convenience, 
Ren-nii calls them Markers.

13:35.980 --> 13:39.520
So, if there's a place with 
one of these Marker things,

13:39.520 --> 13:42.460
that means there was some 
kind of Curiosity there before.

13:42.460 --> 13:44.410
Is that right?

13:45.340 --> 13:46.350
That's right.

13:46.970 --> 13:48.840
You believe me?

13:48.840 --> 13:50.170
Not yet.

13:53.190 --> 13:55.800
<i>This girl is adorable.</i>

13:57.100 --> 14:00.570
But I've decided to try to believe you.

14:00.570 --> 14:01.360
Huh?

14:01.830 --> 14:04.870
You were clearly scared of that Marker.

14:04.870 --> 14:06.780
Your finger was trembling.

14:07.100 --> 14:09.800
But you still explained it to me 
in spite of that, didn't you?

14:10.880 --> 14:12.870
Y-Yes.

14:19.180 --> 14:22.260
How long have you been able 
to see a Marker here?

14:22.260 --> 14:25.060
Since about a month ago.

14:26.260 --> 14:30.550
A red-faced Occhan and an unknown senpai, 
leaving the bathroom together?

14:30.550 --> 14:34.680
This is a huge scoop! 
It'll shake the whole industry!

14:34.680 --> 14:36.570
Are you from some gossip tabloid?

14:37.900 --> 14:40.630
You're being rude to our senpai, Tama-chan!

14:41.320 --> 14:44.250
I'm so sorry, Wakazukuri-senpai.

14:44.250 --> 14:48.160
What? This is the Wakazukuri-senpai 
I've been hearing about?

14:49.380 --> 14:51.740
Occhan! She's your sweetheart, right?

14:51.740 --> 14:52.410
Huh?

14:52.410 --> 14:54.540
Introduce us!

14:54.540 --> 14:56.720
What?

14:58.690 --> 15:00.550
And so...

15:00.940 --> 15:03.560
this is our special guest, 
a first-year in our high school,

15:03.560 --> 15:05.800
Wakazukuri-senpai!

15:05.800 --> 15:07.590
A round of applause!

15:08.400 --> 15:09.830
Hi there!

15:09.830 --> 15:13.550
<i>Yes! This is what I've been waiting for!</i>

15:13.550 --> 15:14.560
It's delicious.

15:14.560 --> 15:16.060
Right? Right?

15:16.060 --> 15:20.760
Mari, no fair! Monopolizing 
Occhan is prohibited by law!

15:20.760 --> 15:22.990
She has to come to me, too!

15:22.990 --> 15:25.190
Mari's lap is better.

15:26.200 --> 15:28.320
I've been rejected!

15:29.450 --> 15:32.280
Hey, have you heard the rumor?

15:32.280 --> 15:33.200
What rumor?

15:33.200 --> 15:37.350
Apparently, Akemi-chan and 
Mika-san from Class 3 kissed.

15:38.540 --> 15:41.230
Akemi? She's going out 
with Hitomi, isn't she?

15:41.230 --> 15:43.240
Could it be an affair?

15:43.240 --> 15:45.710
Outrageous. They'll throw the 
school order into disarray.

15:46.250 --> 15:50.470
And Akemi's the lewd type, so she'll come 
up and go straight for the breasts, y'know?

15:50.470 --> 15:53.350
She hasn't touched mine.

15:53.350 --> 15:56.180
I get hugged a lot.

15:56.180 --> 15:59.030
Nodoka, you definitely shouldn't 
let people do that to you.

16:01.610 --> 16:06.240
Oh! Wakazukuri-senpai is in high school, 
so she should have lots of experience!

16:06.240 --> 16:08.990
Who have you made out with, 
and what was it like?

16:09.310 --> 16:11.440
Tell us your super-sensual 
personal experiences.

16:11.440 --> 16:13.620
Have you experienced a steamy romance?

16:17.180 --> 16:20.220
Well, yes. Of course I have.

16:20.220 --> 16:25.850
I tear up every man that approaches me 
and toss them aside. Tear and toss.

16:27.260 --> 16:30.970
High school students really are amazing.

16:31.760 --> 16:34.510
What about a steamier story?

16:34.740 --> 16:36.640
A super explicit one?

16:36.640 --> 16:40.210
Tama-chan, you're a little too serious 
about this. Why all the enthusiasm?

16:41.220 --> 16:42.770
Well, I mean...

16:43.380 --> 16:47.280
Nothing provocative happens at this school.

16:47.540 --> 16:51.530
There's no bullying at all. It's so peaceful,

16:51.530 --> 16:53.970
it's actually sort of creepy.

16:54.530 --> 16:56.870
There's no bullying at all?

16:56.870 --> 17:02.020
In a school with this many students, 
that'd take a miracle. It's hard to believe.

17:02.020 --> 17:05.120
I think it's nice that it's so peaceful.

17:05.120 --> 17:09.910
But lately, more and more students 
have been failing to attend, right?

17:09.910 --> 17:13.300
Oh, you mean the dribblers?

17:13.300 --> 17:15.160
<i>Finally, what I'm here for.</i>

17:30.320 --> 17:33.320
<b></b>Dribblers

17:30.320 --> 17:33.320
<b></b>Fever

17:30.320 --> 17:33.320
<b></b>Excessive drooling

17:30.320 --> 17:33.320
<b></b>Cause?

17:30.320 --> 17:33.320
<b></b>Symptoms start at school

17:30.320 --> 17:33.320
<b></b>They go home

17:30.320 --> 17:33.320
<b></b>Anywhere
Any time

17:30.320 --> 17:33.320
<b></b>Shut themselves in

17:30.320 --> 17:33.320
<b></b><u>Only students</u>

17:31.790 --> 17:33.320
<i>"Dribblers."</i>

17:33.320 --> 17:37.450
<i>The name of a strange yet frequent 
occurrence at this school.</i>

17:37.450 --> 17:41.580
<i>A student will suddenly have their body 
grow as hot as if it were burning,</i>

17:41.580 --> 17:42.900
<i>and then they'll collapse.</i>

17:43.330 --> 17:47.690
<i>After that, they'll start drooling excessively.</i>

17:48.340 --> 17:50.740
<i>It seems to strike at random times, 
without any pattern,</i>

17:50.740 --> 17:52.840
<i>and no attempt at treatment 
has been effective,</i>

17:52.840 --> 17:55.520
<i>but when the afflicted students 
go home, they get better.</i>

17:55.520 --> 17:59.100
<i>And if they return to school, 
the symptoms return.</i>

17:59.930 --> 18:04.330
<i>That's why those students, fearing 
a relapse, fail to attend school.</i>

18:05.700 --> 18:07.170
I see.

18:10.750 --> 18:13.470
But forget all that. 
How about those sexy stories?

18:13.470 --> 18:15.000
Wakazukuri-senpai?

18:15.000 --> 18:15.870
Hey!

18:17.080 --> 18:19.030
Stop that right now, all of you!

18:20.120 --> 18:21.860
U-Uname-sensei!

18:21.860 --> 18:25.250
I've told you, bullying is wro—

18:27.990 --> 18:30.690
A-Are you all right?

18:34.720 --> 18:38.010
Y-You shouldn't make people 
do things they don't want to!

18:38.010 --> 18:41.390
It isn't like that! 
We were just goofing around!

18:41.390 --> 18:43.270
Don't make excuses!

18:44.250 --> 18:46.210
All of you, go home for today.

18:46.690 --> 18:48.770
And, Wakazukuri-san,

18:48.770 --> 18:51.530
there's something I want to ask you. 
Please come with me.

18:59.860 --> 19:02.220
I want you to tell me honestly.

19:02.710 --> 19:04.290
Tell you what?

19:06.790 --> 19:10.120
You're being bullied, aren't you?

19:15.250 --> 19:17.670
I'm on your side, okay?

19:18.120 --> 19:21.770
You can take it slowly, but won't you 
please tell me what's going on?

19:21.770 --> 19:23.940
No, I'm all right.

19:24.260 --> 19:25.810
Really.

19:26.500 --> 19:30.370
I've had the cruel reality that I don't fit in 
with these young people shoved in my face.

19:30.860 --> 19:32.810
I'm trembling over that. That's all.

19:36.640 --> 19:39.300
I'm sorry for jumping to conclusions!

19:39.300 --> 19:41.330
No, it's all right.

19:42.060 --> 19:45.940
I saw them restraining you 
by your arms, so I panicked.

19:45.940 --> 19:49.330
I messed up big-time. How embarrassing.

19:49.330 --> 19:50.570
Not at all.

19:51.750 --> 19:55.850
Say, Wakazukuri-san, 
do you have a dream or a goal?

19:58.060 --> 19:59.840
A dream, huh?

20:01.310 --> 20:05.600
I've always wanted to be a novelist.

20:07.350 --> 20:13.860
So my dream is to write a real 
page-turner... I suppose.

20:16.390 --> 20:17.670
What's wrong?

20:17.670 --> 20:19.160
That's incredible!

20:19.610 --> 20:24.870
I think it's wonderful that you have such 
a clear dream of becoming a novelist!

20:24.870 --> 20:26.400
I'll be cheering for you!

20:28.270 --> 20:30.140
Th-Thank you.

20:31.130 --> 20:35.670
Being able to support my students 
in their dreams is <i>my</i> dream.

20:35.670 --> 20:38.240
You'll have to let me read 
your novel one day, okay?

20:42.390 --> 20:44.760
She said she's cheering for me!

20:47.780 --> 20:49.860
We've been waiting for you, Senpai!

20:49.860 --> 20:52.200
Now, make with the sexy stories!

20:52.200 --> 20:53.650
Stop it, you oversexed kappa!

21:16.570 --> 21:18.960
Nodoka-chan, please go and get a teacher!

21:18.960 --> 21:20.770
Oto-chan, call for an ambulance!

21:20.770 --> 21:21.430
Right!

21:24.480 --> 21:26.180
What are you doing, Oto-chan?

21:31.530 --> 21:32.440
Don't tell me...

21:33.070 --> 21:34.460
You can see them?

21:35.940 --> 21:37.450
The Markers?

21:39.830 --> 21:43.950
Stones drift. Leaves sink.

21:44.330 --> 21:48.500
Horses moo. Cows neigh.

21:54.830 --> 21:56.460
I told you, didn't I?

21:58.550 --> 22:01.200
Bullying is wrong.

23:35.060 --> 23:41.010
<b>Horns, Bullying, and a Hair Ornament</b>

23:36.280 --> 23:40.020
Next time: "Horns, Bullying, 
and a Hair Ornament."
